00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:38.000
So no white gloves.

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:40.000
I would say go use white gloves.

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:42.000
Because you could be able to slip out of your hands.

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:46.000
I want to say that the biggest thing that I learned

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:49.000
is that we assume that records that were made,

00:05:49.000 --> 00:05:52.000
that maybe we covet or think are really incredible,

00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:54.000
were recorded properly.

00:05:55.000 --> 00:05:58.000
What makes properly or master properly

00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:01.000
or cut properly, printed properly,

00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:03.000
and well they're not.

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:06.000
So when you get a master tape

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:09.000
and you have like a preconceived notion of what that's going to be,

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:11.000
you realize that there are like

00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:14.000
absolutely insane tones on there that make no sense,

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:16.000
or there's no tones,

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:20.000
or whoever was doing the editing or the littering,

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:22.000
or just any of that.

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:25.000
It just was, we didn't do it on purpose,

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:27.000
we did it on drugs.

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:29.000
There was a lot of cocaine back then.

00:06:29.000 --> 00:06:32.000
You just sort of like, wow, this is, you know,

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:35.000
you forget that there's a lot of things that happen in a process

00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:37.000
from recording to mixing to printing,

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:40.000
because again I work with love, open really well.

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:43.000
And some of the stuff that I got into recently

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:45.000
with the Westbound Collection

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:47.000
and some other things we've been in,

00:06:47.000 --> 00:06:49.000
it's absolutely insane.

00:06:49.000 --> 00:06:52.000
And yeah, so the fundamentals are best practice,

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:54.000
but that's just the starting point.

00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:56.000
And then from there it's like how do we figure out

00:06:56.000 --> 00:06:59.000
how to get around those things that we didn't,

00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:01.000
you know, assume either.

00:07:01.000 --> 00:07:03.000
You know, we were joking that we did a lot of drugs back then.

00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:04.000
That is true.

